# The build context, for whichever Dockerfile is built from this directory.
#
# The data directory is the instance's runtime state: the database, and in it
# the fetch cache of IGDB and RAWG responses neither may be redistributed. An
# image that carried it would be a licence breach, not an oversized layer
# (ADR-0019). `**/` because Docker anchors a bare `data/` at the context root,
# and the default database lives in `backend/data/`.
**/data/
**/*.db
**/*.db-*
**/*.sqlite3

# Secrets (rule 7). The example carries no values and documents the variables.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

.git
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/.mypy_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
